c. Socializing Laws and Regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence;
d. Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of services and protection for women and children victims of violence;
(2) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence, the Regional Government provides and organizes services for victims in the form of : a. Establishing and facilitating the implementation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving community elements; b. Encouraging public awareness of the importance of protection for victims.
(3) The Regional Government in providing and organizing services as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

Article 2

The Principles of Services and Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence are :

a. Respect and recognition of equal rights and human dignity;
b. Respect for victims' rights;
c. Gender justice and equality;
d. Non-discriminatory; and
e. Best interests of the victim.

Article 8

(1) Forms of services and protection for victims organized by P3A consist of:

a. Medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of victims carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. Medicolegal services are a form of medical services for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;
c. Psychosocial services are services provided by companions to restore the traumatic condition of victims, including the provision of safe houses to protect victims from various threats and intimidation to victims and provide social support so that victims have self-confidence, strength and independence in solving their problems;
d. Legal services to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process;
e. Economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.
(2) Further provisions regarding the service and protection mechanism as referred to in paragraph (1) are organized according to Standard Operational Procedures (SOP) which will be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

